# Final Canonical V2 artifacts are integrity-checked byte streams.
# Keep LF in every checkout so SHA-256 values in manifest.json are portable.
"data pharmacy/v2/final_canonical/*.jsonl" text eol=lf
"data pharmacy/v2/final_canonical/manifest.json" text eol=lf
# `*` does not match a nested path in attributes.  The RAG artifacts live in
# `final_canonical/rag/`; preserve their signed LF bytes too.
"data pharmacy/v2/final_canonical/**/*.jsonl" text eol=lf
"data pharmacy/v2/final_canonical/**/*.json" text eol=lf

# 2026-08-22 incident: a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true silently
# converted docker-entrypoint.sh's shebang line to CRLF on disk (the
# committed blob was always correct LF-only). `railway up` uploads the local
# working tree as-is, not a git-normalized archive, so that CRLF-corrupted
# copy got baked into the production image -- the kernel then failed to
# exec `/bin/sh\r` as the entrypoint ("exec ... No such file or directory"),
# causing every healthcheck to fail and taking VMEC-04/BE offline for ~9
# minutes until root-caused and redeployed with the line endings fixed.
# `eol=lf` here forces LF regardless of any checkout's core.autocrlf, so
# this exact failure cannot recur for any contributor's local checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
